Hello, here the code for simulating a microlayer with a resolved microlayer and conjugate heat transfer is provided. It is developed based on the phase-change model from [Edoardo's Sandbox](/sandbox/ecipriano/README). The ghost fluid method and conjugate heat transfer have been incorporated. 

## Installation

Currently, these codes are not compatible with the latest version of Basilisk; the version used is from April 2023. You can download this version of Basilisk using darcs:

~~~bash
darcs clone https://basilisk.fr/basilisk --tag='release 23-06-28' --repo-name basilisk-tianlong
~~~

After cloning, you should apply a patch with modifications to the grid that allows the compatibility with my description of solid boundaries:

~~~bash
cd basilisk-tianlong/src
darcs apply solid.patch
~~~

Finally, procced with classic basilisk compilation:

~~~bash
make
~~~